      <!-- ===== MAYFLOWER vs. DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA ===== -->
      <div class="new-section" style="margin-top:72px;">
        <div style="max-width:960px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 22px;">

          <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:28px;">
            <img
              src="/images/sundaylaw/mayflower-1620-religious-freedom-james-white-family-escaping-state-church-tyranny-sundaylaw.jpg"
              alt="Mayflower 1620 — Escaping Religious Tyranny of the State Church"
              loading="lazy"
              style="max-width:720px;width:100%;border-radius:16px;border:2px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.3);display:block;margin:0 auto;"
            />
            <div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--amber);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.07em;">The Mayflower, 1620 &mdash; Fleeing the Church of England&rsquo;s Persecuting Power</div>
          </div>

          <div class="mayflower-content" style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
            <h2 class="serif">The Mayflower vs. the &ldquo;New Rome&rdquo;</h2>
            <p>In 1620, the Pilgrims aboard the Mayflower crossed the Atlantic to escape the persecuting power of the <strong style="color:#f0cf7b;">state church of England</strong> &mdash; an institution that used civil law to compel religious conformity and jailed, fined, and silenced those who dissented. America was founded on the revolutionary idea that no government may dictate faith.</p>
            <p>On April 15, 1904, in <strong style="color:#f0cf7b;">Washington, District of Columbia</strong> &mdash; a city designed in the pattern of Rome, with its Capitol dome, its Obelisk, and its seat of empire &mdash; the <em>same persecuting power</em> the Pilgrims fled was quietly re-clothed in Protestant garb and registered as a corporation.</p>
            <p>The &ldquo;New Rome&rdquo; issued articles of incorporation to a religious body. The church submitted. The state accepted. The union was consummated. The Image of the Papacy was formed &mdash; not by violence, but by paperwork.</p>
            <div class="warn-box">
              &#9888; The pioneers who built the Adventist movement on protest against Rome left their denominations when those denominations refused to reform. Their successors, just 60 years later, incorporated into the very system the pioneers had protested &mdash; right in the capital of &ldquo;New Rome.&rdquo; This is 1SM 204: <em>&ldquo;A new organization would be established.&rdquo;</em>
            </div>
            <div class="quote">
              <p>&ldquo;The Reformers protested against the union of church and state. But the children of the Reformers have returned to Egypt. They build what their fathers pulled down. Heaven marks the movement: it is the image of the beast.&rdquo;</p>
              <cite>— Alonzo T. Jones &amp; E.J. Waggoner, 1888&ndash;1895, consistently</cite>
            </div>

            <div class="quote" style="margin-top:14px;border-color:rgba(220,38,38,0.55);background:rgba(40,5,5,0.7);">
              <p>&ldquo;In a union of Church and State the Church becomes <strong style="color:#fca5a5;">MARRIED</strong>, as it were, to the State&hellip;&rdquo;</p>
              <cite>— Ellen G. White, Letter 51a, 1898</cite>
            </div>

            <div style="margin-top:28px;padding:24px 26px;background:rgba(180,53,53,0.09);border:1px solid rgba(220,38,38,0.3);border-left:4px solid #ef4444;border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;">
              <p style="font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#fef3c7;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 10px;">
                Your great-grandparents' generation crossed an ocean and built a nation to escape exactly this.
              </p>
              <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.82);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 16px;">
                The Pilgrims did not flee a foreign enemy. They fled <em>their own church leadership</em> — men who had taken the arm of the civil state and used it to silence, fine, imprison, and exile anyone who would not conform. They were not fighting pagans. They were fighting men who called themselves Christians, who wore robes, who held titles, and who had signed documents with civil governments giving those governments power over the consciences of the people. Sound familiar?
              </p>
              <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.82);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 16px;">
                It should. Because it is the same pattern that was used against <em>Jesus Himself</em>. The Jews did not personally execute Christ — they brought Him to <strong style="color:#fca5a5;">Rome</strong>. They went to the Roman civil authority, to Pilate, and demanded that the state enforce their religious verdict. <em>&ldquo;We have no king but Caesar&rdquo;</em> (John 19:15). They used civil power to kill the Son of God. His apostles were dragged before magistrates, imprisoned by the state, beheaded at Rome's command — all at the instigation of a religious leadership that had joined hands with the empire.
              </p>
              <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.82);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 16px;">
                Do we think we are better than our Master? <em>&ldquo;The disciple is not above his master, nor the servant above his lord.&rdquo;</em> (Matthew 10:24). The same Rome that crucified Christ is alive today. Its seat has moved — but its method has not. <strong style="color:#fca5a5;">New Rome is the District of Columbia</strong> — laid out by a Freemason, its Capitol dome mirroring St. Peter's Basilica, its Washington Monument an Egyptian obelisk towering over Caesar's capital. And on April 15, 1904, a man entrusted to keep the faith sold out and hired signors — his hirelings — to sign the corporation papers in the District of Columbia. It was not the church as a body, but an apostate false shepherd wolf who betrayed the trust and led the flock into bondage.
              </p>
              <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.82);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 16px;">
                On April 15, 1904, <strong style="color:#fca5a5;">that same act was performed again</strong> — in Washington, D.C. — by men who called themselves Seventh-day Adventists. The Mayflower generation left everything to be free. Their spiritual heirs handed that freedom back — with a pen, in a corporation filing, to the government of Caesar's capital city.
              </p>
              <p style="font-size:0.95rem;font-weight:700;color:#fef3c7;line-height:1.75;margin:0;">
                If that does not wake you up, read it again.
              </p>
            </div>

