      <!-- ===== THREE UNCLEAN SPIRITS — MARANATHA P.190 ===== -->
      <div class="new-section" style="margin-top:72px;">
        <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 22px;">

          <!-- Scripture header -->
          <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:36px;">
            <div style="display:inline-block;padding:5px 18px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.35);color:#fcd34d;font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:16px;">Revelation 16:13–14</div>
            <blockquote style="font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2.5vw,1.65rem);color:#fef3c7;line-height:1.75;font-style:italic;margin:0;padding:0 24px;">
              &ldquo;And I saw three unclean spirits like frogs come out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet. For they are the spirits of devils, working miracles, which go forth unto the kings of the earth and of the whole world, to gather them to the battle of that great day of God Almighty.&rdquo;
            </blockquote>
            <p style="color:#9ca3af;font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:10px;">Revelation 16:13, 14</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Divider -->
          <div style="width:60px;height:2px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,rgba(212,165,55,0.5),transparent);margin:0 auto 40px;"></div>

          <!-- Quote 1 -->
          <div style="margin-bottom:32px;padding:28px 32px;background:rgba(20,10,0,0.55);border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.2);border-left:4px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.6);border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;">
            <p style="font-size:1.05rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.92);line-height:1.9;margin:0 0 14px;font-style:italic;">
              &ldquo;By the decree enforcing the institution of the papacy in violation of the law of God, our nation [the United States] will disconnect herself fully from righteousness. When Protestantism shall stretch her hand across the gulf to grasp the hand of the Roman power, when she shall reach over the abyss to clasp hands with spiritualism, when, under the influence of this <strong style="color:#fef3c7;font-style:normal;">threefold union</strong>, our country shall repudiate every principle of its Constitution as a Protestant and republican government, and shall make provision for the propagation of papal falsehoods and delusions, then we may know that the time has come for the marvelous working of Satan and that the end is near.&rdquo;
            </p>
            <cite style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#9ca3af;font-style:normal;">— Ellen G. White, <em>Testimonies for the Church</em>, vol. 5, p. 451</cite>
          </div>

          <!-- Quote 2 -->
          <div style="margin-bottom:32px;padding:28px 32px;background:rgba(20,10,0,0.55);border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.2);border-left:4px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.6);border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;">
            <p style="font-size:1.05rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.92);line-height:1.9;margin:0 0 14px;font-style:italic;">
              &ldquo;Through the two great errors, the immortality of the soul and Sunday sacredness, Satan will bring the people under his deceptions. While the former lays the foundation of spiritualism, the latter creates a bond of sympathy with Rome. The Protestants of the United States will be foremost in stretching their hands across the gulf to grasp the hand of spiritualism; they will reach over the abyss to clasp hands with the Roman power; and under the influence of this threefold union, this country will follow in the steps of Rome in trampling on the rights of conscience&hellip;
              <br><br>
              Papists, Protestants, and worldlings will alike accept the form of godliness without the power, and they will see in this union a grand movement for the conversion of the world and the ushering in of the long-expected millennium.&rdquo;
            </p>
            <cite style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#9ca3af;font-style:normal;">— Ellen G. White, <em>The Great Controversy</em>, pp. 588, 589</cite>
          </div>

          <!-- Quote 3 -->
          <div style="margin-bottom:0;padding:28px 32px;background:rgba(20,10,0,0.55);border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.2);border-left:4px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.6);border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;">
            <p style="font-size:1.05rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.92);line-height:1.9;margin:0 0 14px;font-style:italic;">
              &ldquo;When our nation [the United States] shall so abjure the principles of its government as to enact a Sunday law, Protestantism will in this act <strong style="color:#fca5a5;font-style:normal;">join hands with popery</strong>; it will be nothing else than giving life to the tyranny which has long been eagerly watching its opportunity to spring again into active despotism.&rdquo;
            </p>
            <cite style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#9ca3af;font-style:normal;">— Ellen G. White, <em>Testimonies for the Church</em>, vol. 5, p. 712</cite>
          </div>

          <!-- Source label -->
          <p style="text-align:center;margin-top:22px;font-size:0.8rem;color:#6b7280;font-style:italic;">From <em>Maranatha</em>, p. 190</p>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== HABAKKUK / 1850 CHART EXCERPT ===== -->
      <div class="new-section" style="margin-top:72px;">
        <div style="max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 22px;">
          <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:28px;">
            <div style="display:inline-block;padding:5px 16px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.3);color:#fcd34d;font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:12px;">1850 Prophetic Chart — Primary Source Excerpt</div>
            <h2 style="font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem);color:#fef3c7;margin:0 0 10px;">Habakkuk 2:2–3 &mdash; Written Upon Tables</h2>
            <p style="color:#9ca3af;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;">The 1850 Prophetic Chart opens with the command of God to Habakkuk — <em>"Write the vision, and make it plain upon tables, that he may run that readeth it."</em> The pioneers understood this as their commission.</p>
          </div>

          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:24px;">
            <img
              src="/images/1904-image-of-papacy/habakkuk-2-2-3-1850-prophecy-chart-excerpt-image-of-the-papacy.jpg"
              alt="Habakkuk 2:2–3 — 1850 Prophetic Chart Excerpt — Image of the Papacy"
              loading="lazy"
              style="max-width:680px;width:100%;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.3);display:block;"
            />
          </div>

          <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:28px;">
            <a
              href="/prophecy-charts"
              style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:11px 26px;background:rgba(212,165,55,0.12);border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.45);border-radius:10px;color:#fcd34d;font-size:0.88rem;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0.03em;transition:background 0.2s;"
            >
              View the 1843 &amp; 1850 Prophetic Charts &rarr;
            </a>
          <div style="background:rgba(212,165,55,0.06);border-left:4px solid #d4a537;border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;padding:22px 26px;margin-bottom:24px;">
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.12em;color:#fcd34d;margin-bottom:10px;">Ellen G. White — Letter 57, 1896 &bull; Manuscript Releases, Vol. 12, p. 113</div>
            <blockquote style="font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:1.15rem;font-style:italic;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.92);line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 10px;">
              &ldquo;There is need of a much closer study of the word of God&hellip; We may have less to say in some lines, in regard to the Roman power and the papacy, but we should call attention to what the prophets and apostles have written&hellip; The Holy Spirit has so shaped matters&hellip; as to teach that the human agent is to be kept out of sight&hellip; and the Lord God of heaven and His law are to be exalted.&rdquo;
            </blockquote>
            <cite style="display:block;font-size:0.8rem;color:#9ca3af;font-style:normal;font-weight:600;">— Ellen G. White, Letter 57, 1896 (Manuscript Releases, Vol. 12, p. 113)</cite>
          </div>

          <div style="background:rgba(239,68,68,0.07);border:1px solid rgba(239,68,68,0.28);border-radius:14px;padding:22px 26px;margin-bottom:28px;">
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.12em;color:#fca5a5;margin-bottom:10px;">What This Means Today</div>
            <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:rgba(254,243,199,0.85);line-height:1.85;margin:0;">
              Ellen White wrote in 1896 that we would have <em>less</em> to say about the Roman power and papacy — because the danger had moved closer. The church had begun building what she warned against from within. By 1904 it was complete. The three civil corporations formed between 1887 and 1904 — the <strong style="color:#fef3c7;">General Conference Association of Seventh-day Adventists</strong> (Michigan, 1887), the New York Foreign Mission Board, and the <strong style="color:#fca5a5;">General Conference Corporation of Seventh-day Adventists</strong> (Washington, D.C., April 15, 1904) — are the union of church and state she spent her life warning against, now wearing the name of the Advent movement.
            </p>
